I've been playing Nethack for many, many years, and am thrilled to
finally get to post one of these.  I had just killed my previous
promising character near the castle in a very stupid way, by eating
while satiated and choking.  I knew I was close to victory, and
resolved to play a much more careful game the next time around.  And
it worked!  My Valkyrie made it to the final altar with the Amulet and
I finally get to post my YAFAP.

This wasn't a nuanced game.  I was thoroughly spoiled, took a strong
class, raised all my statistics higher than necessary, genocided
everything that typically causes me trouble, and ignored all conducts.
No apologies for playing for a win, or for my endgame luck.

The RNG had a very straightforward game in store for me, which helped
greatly.  I didn't get any big early presents, but I didn't face any
challenges, either.  Some notes from the game:

- I was burdened for much of the early game.  I got through Sokoban,
  through much of the Gnomish Mines, and to maybe level 15 of the main
  dungeon before getting a first wish.  I strongly considered wishing
  for gauntlets of power to both help deal with the encumberance and
  make Mjollnir even better, but instead I went for GDSM.  When I put
  it on, I realized it was the bronze plate mail I found early causing
  all my weight problems.  I'll have to watch that next time.

- It took me a very long time to get fire resistance.  I even did the
  castle before the quest, waiting for some monster, any monster to
  give me fire resistance, but eventually I had to do the quest
  without it.  I don't recall with certainty when I finally got it,
  but I have to imagine it was during the quest.

- Very deep in the dungeon I found a large leprechaun hall that made
  me rich.  After that I made my last trip to Minetown, as I had
  enough money to get my naked AC to 1 and clean out all the shops I
  knew of.  At this point I stopped carrying money and gems.

- If the RNG was indifferent in the early game, it loved me in the
  late game.  Including the one at Vlad's tower, I found four amulets
  of life saving and two magic lamps in hell, though I never used the
  amulets.

- I overprepared for the return trip, digging tunnels five spaces wide
  from stairway to stairway all the way up.  The time was spent well,
  however: I had left a few incubi alive in the dungeon when my stats
  weren't good enough to abuse them.  By the time I started digging
  tunnels, my stats were maxed out.  So I had the incubi chase me down
  the stairs while I worked, and I advanced all the way to level 30
  that way.  Digging helped pass the time while they had headaches.

- Rodney presented very little challenge.  Somehow I only ever faced
  him directly twice!  I got the guaranteed appearances, but he never
  popped in to fight me.  He summoned baddies for me to step around,
  and he cursed a few of my items, but I was not short on holy water.

- The Astral Plane went just as easily.  I decided to start at the
  middle altar, guarded by Pestilence.  A ring of conflict made things
  go more easily, and I only get made ill once.  I reached the altar,
  and was giddy to see it was Odin's.

